1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
["Mr. Tailor" playing] ♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,677
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

4
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,141
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

5
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:17,308
♪ <i>In the world's mess</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,852
[Olga, in English] <i>Hello. Friend?</i>

7
00:00:18,935 --> 00:00:20,979
<i>I thought of something</i>
<i>we can make money from.</i>

8
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,314
[Charmi] <i>Olga is an actress.</i>

9
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:25,358
She looks familiar to me.

10
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:28,528
<i>Abot-Kamay na Pangarap.</i>
Yes, she was an extra there.

11
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:29,571
[T-Bak] From the start,

12
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:32,198
- you should've gone for Karla instead!
- [Billy] Exactly!

13
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:35,076
- Won't Cathy get mad at you?
- Don't worry about that.

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,578
[Gavin, in English] <i>Where are we going?</i>

15
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:37,579
That's my mom.

16
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:40,331
[Olga] <i>A hundred thousand is nothing</i>
<i>compared to what we'll earn today.</i>

17
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,459
[Ibyang] <i>Mama, is that you?</i>

18
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:45,462
[in English] Of course,
my darling. [chuckles]

19
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,046
[in English] I'm quite busy right now.

20
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,673
Maybe she's just in character.

21
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,884
[Olga] <i>My ex left that after</i>

22
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:52,927
he dumped me for another woman.

23
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,471
[Charmi] <i>Only four exist.</i>

24
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:55,972
- [Olga, in English] Yes.
- Three are in museums.

25
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,390
[man, in English] <i>It's already sold.</i>

26
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,101
[Atoy, in Visayan] <i>Is the Mayor in there?</i>

27
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,062
<i>Can I tell him something?</i>

28
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,354
[security guard] <i>Do you not have</i>
<i>an appointment with him?</i>

29
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:04,939
[security guard, in Visayan]
I'm sorry, sir,

30
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,525
but we have strict rules here.
The Mayor's receiving death threats.

31
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:10,111
[man, in English] Oh, it's fake!

32
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:11,529
[in English] I got scammed!

33
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:13,531
[in English] Mama?

34
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:16,826
[Ibyang] <i>Mama scammed the man,</i>
<i>that's why he chased her.</i>

35
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:20,246
PREVIOUSLY

36
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,084
[grunts and groans]

37
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,753
- Ouch!
- [Olga] Fool!

38
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,338
I'm just helping you.

39
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:29,506
[Olga] Get out of here!

40
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:32,300
[man, in English] Maybe it's her!
Stop her!

41
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:33,551
[Emerson, in English] My love!

42
00:01:34,677 --> 00:01:36,221
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

43
00:01:36,304 --> 00:01:37,639
- Oh, oh.
- My love, don't leave me!

44
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:38,598
Stay here!

45
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:40,725
- Don't go.
- [man, in English] Where's the girl?

46
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:42,977
[security guard] That woman is a thief!

47
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:45,021
- [security guard] Where did she go?
- [Emerson] A thief? Eh--

48
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:47,023
- [Emerson] Yes, she stole my heart.
- Where did she go?

49
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:49,317
Over there! I hope she comes back.

50
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,319
- Find the bag!
- [in English] How about my money?!

51
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:53,446
- [man, in English] Where is it?!
- [Emerson] I don't know.

52
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,656
I don't know what money
you're talking about--

53
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:55,865
Sir, is this your bag?

54
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:57,659
That's her bag.

55
00:01:57,742 --> 00:01:59,244
Wait, that's her bag.

56
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:00,829
[man, in English] My money is here.

57
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:03,331
I don't know. I just saw it here.

58
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:04,332
[in English] My money is here.

59
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:06,459
Wow! Oh, good thing. It's in her bag.

60
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:07,502
[barangay police] Just explain
at the community hall.

61
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,546
- [Emerson] Huh? Why should I go?
- [barangay police] Come with us!

62
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:10,713
- [overlapping chatter]
- Stop pretending.

63
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:11,965
You're an accomplice of the woman scammer!

64
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:12,924
- I'm not--
- Come with us!

65
00:02:13,007 --> 00:02:14,259
I just saw her today!

66
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:15,510
- You're an accomplice!
- No, I'm not!

67
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:17,178
No, wait, my love!

68
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:21,015
- [clamoring]
- [action music playing]

69
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,350
[music fades]

70
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:31,192
[in English] Are you sure
we are in the right place?

71
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,944
[in English] Our intel told us

72
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:36,281
that the decoder of this town
is the mayor's niece.

73
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:37,782
[in English] So, she might be here.

74
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:42,954
[suspicious music playing]

75
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:47,125
[in English] This is the man who broke
into the ambassador's office.

76
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:51,004
[in English] He might be here too.

77
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,549
[in English] Take a good look at him.

78
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:57,135
[in English] But be careful.

79
00:02:57,927 --> 00:03:00,305
[in English] This man has many faces

80
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,516
and can be very dangerous.

81
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:17,697
[music fades]

82
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:39,594
[in Visayan] Oh,
the secretary of the mayor said

83
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:43,348
to wait for their message
before we go to their house.

84
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:46,059
I think someone else is performing.

85
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:48,519
[performer 2, in Visayan] How about Jun?

86
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,647
[in Visayan] I even brought his costume.

87
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:53,233
[in Visayan] He abandoned us.

88
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:58,655
[performer 1, in Visayan] Okay.
This is what we shall do.

89
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:01,991
[in Visayan] Let's just practice
even if it's just the six of us.

90
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:04,327
[performer 2, in Visayan] Okay! Let's go!

91
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:06,955
[in Visayan] So our efforts
won't be in vain.

92
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:09,624
[suspicious music playing]

93
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:12,460
[performer 1, in Visayan]
There's a vacant space there.

94
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,586
[performer 3, in Visayan] Drinks, please.

95
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:16,506
[performer 1, in Visayan] There!
We can practice here.

96
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:17,632
[Atoy] Boss, here's my payment.

97
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:19,968
[music fades]

98
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:23,096
[suave theme music playing]

99
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:49,247
[music fades]

100
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:53,584
Karla, have you spoken to Brother Atoy
after he found out everything?

101
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:55,878
Not yet, he's not here. He's on a mission.

102
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,255
Thank you, by the way.

103
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:00,174
Why are you thanking me?

104
00:05:00,258 --> 00:05:02,260
We're the ones bothering you.

105
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:05,555
No reason. I'm just happy today.

106
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,140
[in English] You don't understand.

107
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:08,266
No, really.

108
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:10,351
Be straight with me.

109
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,353
I've been weirded out by you.

110
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:15,815
You keep smiling,
and you're spending time with us.

111
00:05:16,357 --> 00:05:18,985
- Gavin, are you sick?
- [Gavin chuckles]

112
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:20,403
[sentimental music playing]

113
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,196
No, I'm not sick.

114
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:26,075
But you know, what you're doing now

115
00:05:26,909 --> 00:05:30,413
made me realize
I don't really like Cathy.

116
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,123
Then who?

117
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:33,833
[music fades]

118
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:35,001
- Who--
- [Cita] Karla.

119
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,422
[unsettling music playing]

120
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:43,426
Young man, you shouldn't be coming here.

121
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:46,179
Didn't Atoy forbid you from doing so?

122
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:48,556
I'll go now.

123
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,518
Mom, why are you like that to Gavin?

124
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:56,939
Karla, let me remind you.

125
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:59,609
He's Red Regalia's son.

126
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:01,778
[Cita] He's the one
who killed your father.

127
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,738
He already clashed with Atoy.

128
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:07,909
What if his father sent him to snoop here?

129
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:09,827
To get back at Atoy.

130
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:14,707
Don't be swayed by his smiles and charm,

131
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:16,501
even if he's your friend.

132
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:20,213
Remember. He's a Regalia.

133
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:22,131
They're bad people.

134
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:26,594
And in the end,
he'll still choose his family.

135
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:33,643
[music fades]

136
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:38,731
Hey, Olga.

137
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,734
So? Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

138
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:44,570
I'm fine.

139
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:47,073
I hadn't gone far
when I heard the shouting.

140
00:06:47,156 --> 00:06:50,493
I thought something happened to you!
Are you okay?!

141
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:51,410
‪No.

142
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:55,081
The watch was immediately exposed as fake.
I hadn't even left yet.

143
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:58,835
Ha? Hmm.

144
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:01,963
No, no. It's fine.

145
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:04,674
What's important is you
and the money are safe.

146
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:08,052
[pensive music playing]

147
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:09,011
Oh?

148
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:12,515
I thought I could escape.

149
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:14,517
But…

150
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:17,019
that fool bumped into me.

151
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:20,606
The money was left inside the bag.

152
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:22,024
Oh.

153
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:24,610
For real?

154
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,990
Olga!

155
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:32,410
[grunts]

156
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:33,911
[music fades]

157
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,040
[car door closes]

158
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:50,845
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

159
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,737
[music fades]

160
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,907
Ibyang is changing
her clothes in the room.

161
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:14,494
She already told me
what happened at the mall.

162
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:16,370
Did you see her mom?

163
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:20,041
But Ibyang seems sure that she saw her.

164
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:25,171
[Karla] Brother!

165
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,173
I thought you'd follow.

166
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:29,634
- You didn't come.
- I was there.

167
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:34,096
I came, but I ended up
at the barangay hall because

168
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:38,226
I was accused of being an accomplice
of that woman scammer.

169
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:40,102
Unbelievable.

170
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:41,854
The one who ran from the mall?

171
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:44,315
Yes, the one who

172
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:46,734
sold the fake watch.

173
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:49,195
We were at the mall when she got exposed!

174
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:51,322
- [Emerson] Oh?
- But I didn't see her face.

175
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,158
So, what does she look like?

176
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:58,538
She's beautiful, sexy, looks rich.

177
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:01,457
[pensive music playing]

178
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:05,378
- Ame, where is Ibyang?
- [Ame] Oh!

179
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,505
We're going home.

180
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:11,467
Ah, like that. She looks like her.

181
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:15,054
[sneaky music playing]

182
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,431
That's…

183
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:19,058
That was… you.

184
00:09:19,141 --> 00:09:20,643
It's her.

185
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:25,648
You're the woman earlier
at the mall parking lot.

186
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:27,483
[in English] My love.

187
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:31,195
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

188
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:37,159
You're really her.

189
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,328
You're her.

190
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,455
You just don't have your mole, but…

191
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:44,166
I can't be mistaken.

192
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:47,420
[sneaky music playing]

193
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:50,756
I can tell, I can never go wrong,

194
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:54,051
when it comes to my loves.

195
00:09:56,846 --> 00:10:00,641
Ame, what… What are you saying?

196
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,268
Who is this crazy person?

197
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:05,980
You're being too harsh, calling me crazy.

198
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:10,985
I'm the one who will be
your future husband slash fiancé.

199
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:13,779
But you hurt me.

200
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:16,407
[in English] Straight here, to my heart.

201
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:19,827
Don't deny it.

202
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:22,580
I know it's really you. Don't deny it.

203
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:25,166
You just… your mole in the mall.

204
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,251
Ah, what… how?

205
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:28,169
Emerson!

206
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:30,880
Stop it. [grunts] What are you doing?

207
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:32,882
What's wrong with you?
Maybe she just looks like the woman.

208
00:10:32,965 --> 00:10:34,550
She's Ibyang's mom!

209
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,344
- Huh?
- This.

210
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:37,845
Yes.

211
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,639
How could that happen?

212
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,766
I was at a taping all day.

213
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:44,894
And I don't know you. I just saw you now.

214
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:47,271
Okay? Please, I'm tired.

215
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:52,777
Where's Ibyang? Tell her we're going home.

216
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,236
I'll just wait outside.

217
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,946
Okay, I'll call her upstairs.

218
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:57,406
[sneaky music playing]

219
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,449
[Emerson mutters]

220
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,910
[in English] My love.

221
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,703
- [Karla] It's okay, brother.
- [Ame] Stop it already.

222
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:04,455
- [in English] How's your heart?
- [Ame] Hey.

223
00:11:07,833 --> 00:11:08,751
[Ame] Ibyang?

224
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:09,752
OPEN
COME IN!

225
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:10,878
[in English] My love…

226
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:14,965
[in English] Someday. Someday.

227
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,175
[music fades]

228
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:21,972
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

229
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,353
[music fades]

230
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:28,896
Let me see what you're doing.

231
00:11:28,979 --> 00:11:30,022
- [Audrey, in English] Dad.
- [in English] Yes? What?

232
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:32,608
Um, here's your stuff that they kept
when you were hospitalized.

233
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:34,652
I already talked to your doctor.

234
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,195
He said you're cleared.

235
00:11:36,779 --> 00:11:38,739
[in English] Wow! Then it's official.

236
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,991
I can travel now.

237
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,535
- [Audrey, in English] Yes!
- [chuckles]

238
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:43,536
Yay!

239
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:45,830
Will you come with us, Grandpa?

240
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:47,206
[in English] Of course!

241
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:53,421
[in English] Wait, uh…

242
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,966
Where's my ring? It's not here.

243
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:01,345
[in English] Found it.

244
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:02,847
[Dmitri] Oh.

245
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:05,141
[pensive music playing]

246
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,183
[Janine, in English] Mommy.

247
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:09,603
When are we leaving?

248
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,231
Later, tomorrow?

249
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:15,109
We'll get your visa first, child.

250
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:17,736
It's already scheduled,
and once we have that,

251
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:19,822
we'll buy the ticket.

252
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:21,449
[in English] Where to?

253
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,409
[in English] Anywhere in the US.

254
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:26,579
Wherever my grandchild wants to go.

255
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:28,539
That's where we'll go.

256
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:31,500
So, where? Where do you
want to go, grandchild?

257
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:34,795
To Disneyland!

258
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,130
[in English] Sorry.

259
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:38,299
[chuckles, in English] Disneyland, okay.

260
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:40,009
[music fades]

261
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,218
[in English] Disneyland it is.

262
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:47,433
[suspicious music playing]

263
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:56,650
[Audrey] Janine?

264
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:58,152
[music swells]

265
00:12:58,235 --> 00:12:59,403
Child?

266
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:00,488
[in English] Mommy.

267
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:03,157
- Mommy.
- [in English] Janine, what's wrong?

268
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,660
[in English] Grandchild, are you okay?

269
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:09,747
Mommy, let's go inside. Please, Mommy?

270
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,916
- Let's go inside, quickly.
- Okay, okay. Let's go.

271
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:12,958
[in English] Let's go.

272
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:15,503
[music swells]

273
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:22,843
[music fades]

274
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,137
[unsettling music playing]

275
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:26,138
My child.

276
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:29,850
[hushes]

277
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:32,019
[in English] It's just
the two of us now, okay?

278
00:13:35,731 --> 00:13:36,774
Child.

279
00:13:38,692 --> 00:13:40,444
What happened?

280
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,281
Why did you cry all of a sudden?

281
00:13:45,616 --> 00:13:46,700
[in English] Tell me.

282
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:49,662
[in English] What happened?

283
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:51,038
[music fades]

284
00:13:51,121 --> 00:13:51,997
Mom…

285
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:55,501
[in English] You look like
you've seen a ghost.

286
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:58,796
[pensive music playing]

287
00:13:58,879 --> 00:13:59,547
[Mongki] What now?!

288
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,882
[Aldrin] She evaded me.
Didn't you run into her?

289
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,759
No! Where is she?

290
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:08,097
[music swells]

291
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,433
- Hey! Hey!
- [gunshots]

292
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:12,768
No one follows!

293
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:14,603
You thought you could escape from me, huh!

294
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:17,731
Oh, it's like that, Mommy.

295
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:18,857
[sniffles]

296
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,402
What do you mean?

297
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:26,615
Because when I saw

298
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:29,535
the shoes of Uncle Red's friend,

299
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:33,080
they were the same shoes

300
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:34,790
as the one who tried to take me before.

301
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,836
I thought they were going
to take me, Mommy.

302
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,921
I got scared, Mommy.

303
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,631
Janine, don't be scared. Okay?

304
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:45,134
[in English] You're safe.

305
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:50,264
[tense music playing]

306
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:57,521
Where's Dad?

307
00:14:58,314 --> 00:14:59,899
[in English] Mmm, he left. How's Janine?

308
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,192
She's still crying.

309
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:05,195
She said she suddenly remembered the one
who tried to kidnap her.

310
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,947
[suspicious music playing]

311
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:09,033
She suddenly remembered? That's weird.

312
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,452
[in English] It's not weird, Red.

313
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:15,331
The child was traumatized,
and what triggered her…

314
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:18,417
were your shoes!

315
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,878
Oh? Why my shoes?

316
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,089
There are lots of shoes like that.

317
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:27,134
Poor child, if she'll always
be triggered by shoes.

318
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:28,719
[in English] She needs professional help.

319
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:31,180
Tell me.

320
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:35,142
Do you know the man
who tried to take my child?

321
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:36,644
What?

322
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:38,312
Why are you asking me like that?

323
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:39,730
Just answer me.

324
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:42,900
Why would I know him?
I'm not a child trafficker.

325
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,401
[music fades]

326
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:45,527
Are you sure?

327
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:50,699
[rousing music playing]

328
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:58,791
[indicator ticking]

329
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:03,754
- [Olga] Oh, dear.
- [car door clicks open]

330
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:07,007
[Olga sighs]

331
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:07,925
[car door clicks shut]

332
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:12,179
[footsteps approaching]

333
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:15,849
Ibyang, what are you doing outside?

334
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,977
Come on. Get inside the car.

335
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:20,604
Where did you really go earlier?

336
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:22,690
[suspicious music playing]

337
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:24,274
In-- Tanay!

338
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:28,821
What about you?
Why are you talking to me like that, huh?

339
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:31,281
Gosh, you sound like the parent.

340
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:33,534
Come on. Let's go.

341
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:36,662
I'm not going with you.

342
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:40,207
Why? Are you mad at me?

343
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:42,793
You're a liar!

344
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:45,504
It's impossible you're my mom.

345
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,881
You're a scammer!

346
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:50,718
[music intensifies]

347
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:55,597
What are you saying?
I'm not a member of the syndicate.

348
00:16:58,225 --> 00:17:00,686
[Red, in English] You know what?
You also need professional help.

349
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:01,937
Go to therapy.

350
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:05,566
You're even doubting your family now.
You're too paranoid.

351
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,736
I know the history of this family.

352
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,821
[in English] I just want to make sure.

353
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:19,121
[music fades]

354
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:23,792
Prick!

355
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,044
[mysterious music playing]

356
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:26,920
What was that? The child recognized you.

357
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:28,005
No!

358
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,840
It was Aldrin
who chased after her back then.

359
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:31,467
Why did she recognize your shoes?

360
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:32,426
I don't know.

361
00:17:32,509 --> 00:17:35,095
I don't even remember what I wore then.
I have lots of shoes!

362
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:43,187
Boss, give us alcohol to relax.

363
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,189
This coffee just made us more nervous.

364
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:50,861
You know, your sister is just baiting you.

365
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:54,615
You even said yourself,
Audrey is just paranoid.

366
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:58,327
[tense music playing]

367
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,164
[sighs]

368
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,584
How many times do I have to tell you?

369
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:08,504
I'm your mother. You're my daughter!

370
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:11,006
What do you want me to do
so you'll believe me, Ibyang?

371
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:17,387
Just kidding, Mama!

372
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:20,432
What? I'm good at acting, right?

373
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:24,978
[light music playing]

374
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:29,441
You really are my mom,

375
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:31,527
- because I take after you.
- Hmm?

376
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,030
Come here.

377
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,698
This is just a secret, okay?

378
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,869
I used to be a scammer too.

379
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:43,455
Hmm? Really?

380
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:45,791
Mmm-hmm. Yes.

381
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:50,212
But when we lived with Tatoy,

382
00:18:50,712 --> 00:18:52,005
I was forbidden to do that

383
00:18:52,589 --> 00:18:54,258
because it's bad.

384
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:58,512
So, I hope you don't do that anymore.

385
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:01,140
So, now? What will happen to us?

386
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,474
Nothing!

387
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:06,061
This is the only job I know.

388
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:09,857
And it's so hard to land roles
in my career.

389
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:12,985
So sometimes,

390
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:16,405
it's unavoidable to do something wrong.

391
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:18,323
[melancholic music playing]

392
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,409
That's okay.

393
00:19:20,492 --> 00:19:22,661
No one's perfect.

394
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:27,624
Except for your beauty
and your acting skills.

395
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:33,088
[Ibyang] It's true!

396
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:37,217
And I'm sure you'll be famous too.

397
00:19:37,801 --> 00:19:41,597
[in English] Just try and try
until you succeed!

398
00:19:42,347 --> 00:19:44,975
But don't scam people.

399
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:49,062
Because you might end up in jail.

400
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:51,773
I want to be with you.

401
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:56,695
On Christmas, on my birthday.

402
00:19:57,362 --> 00:20:00,449
So many occasions have already passed.

403
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:04,703
Go on.

404
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,081
Get your things inside.
I'll wait for you here, okay?

405
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:08,999
Mm-hmm.

406
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:23,305
[music fades]

407
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:28,727
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

408
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,236
[gasps]

409
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:38,779
[sharp exhale]

410
00:20:38,862 --> 00:20:40,322
Godfather, sorry.

411
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:41,907
[in Visayan] I got a fright.

412
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:43,575
[in Visayan] What, Godfather?

413
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:44,826
[in Visayan] I am inviting you.

414
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:47,079
[in Visayan] Maybe you wanted
to watch the performance outside.

415
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:50,123
[in Visayan] Someone might see me.

416
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:55,045
[in Visayan] I know you're scared
that the ambassador will see you.

417
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:56,630
[in Visayan] You're safe here.

418
00:20:58,006 --> 00:20:59,841
[in Visayan] I know, Godfather, but…

419
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:04,680
[in Visayan] Can I stay here?
I feel safer here.

420
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:07,349
[pensive music playing]

421
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:09,643
[in English] Excuse me, Mayor?

422
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:12,396
[in Visayan] Should we have
our guests' associates picked up?

423
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:13,939
Okay.

424
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:20,654
[music fades]

425
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:27,077
[sneaky music playing]

426
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:30,580
[in Visayan] Hey, boss,
my associates are in there.

427
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,333
[in Visayan] I just parked my car.

428
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:35,669
[in Visayan] You should go and join them.

429
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:36,628
Yes.

430
00:21:37,337 --> 00:21:38,797
[tires screeching]

431
00:21:42,926 --> 00:21:44,511
[music fades]

432
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:48,724
[in English] We will proceed as planned.

433
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:52,352
[in English] But remember,
the decoder must be taken alive.

434
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:54,771
[pensive music playing]

435
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:57,649
[in English] We will enter
from the side, but be fast.

436
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:00,277
[in Russian] Get ready.

437
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,445
[in English] Get ready.

438
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:07,576
[tense music playing]

439
00:22:09,369 --> 00:22:10,412
Thank you.

440
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:20,756
[door lock clicks]

441
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:24,009
[sneaky music playing]

442
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:48,366
What's this?

443
00:23:09,346 --> 00:23:10,222
What's this?

444
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:12,974
[tense music playing]

445
00:23:15,435 --> 00:23:17,062
[in English] What the hell, Red?

446
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:21,817
[music swells]

447
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,443
[in English] Oh my God.

448
00:23:24,444 --> 00:23:25,695
[music fades]

449
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:28,573
[Atoy] Sister.

450
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:30,242
[in Visayan] Where's the bathroom?

451
00:23:30,867 --> 00:23:32,953
[in Visayan] Go through that door,

452
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:35,956
turn right, and the CR is there.

453
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:49,553
[tense music playing]

454
00:23:58,603 --> 00:23:59,646
[music fades]

455
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:03,275
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

456
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:12,367
[gunshots]

457
00:24:12,450 --> 00:24:13,702
Sir, they're here, sir!

458
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:15,245
[armed man on radio]
<i>We're about to catch them, sir!</i>

459
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:18,707
[thuds]

460
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:21,168
[thumping and thudding]

461
00:24:21,251 --> 00:24:24,880
UP NEXT

462
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,257
[tranquilizer gunshots]

463
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:30,802
Dear, maybe you should focus
on Ibyang first.

464
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:32,846
Make peace with her.

465
00:24:32,929 --> 00:24:34,347
Maybe you're right.

466
00:24:34,431 --> 00:24:37,893
[Olga] <i>The kid isn't doing anything wrong</i>
<i>for me to treat her like that.</i>

467
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:41,396
This is the first time I've had
such a beautiful doll.

468
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:43,857
Did I tell you to take this?!

469
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:46,776
I don't know
how you can stomach doing this?

470
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,612
[Audrey] Even to my own child.

471
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,238
Dad needs to see this.

472
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:52,782
He knows this. No one will defend you.

473
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:54,367
[security guard, in English] <i>What are we</i>
<i>going to do with them?</i>

474
00:24:54,451 --> 00:24:57,454
[in English] We have to find out
who he works for.

475
00:24:57,537 --> 00:24:59,164
[security officer, in English]
<i>What if he doesn't talk?</i>

476
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:03,168
[Samir, in English] <i>Then we will squeeze</i>
<i>this information from them.</i>

477
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:06,880
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

478
00:25:06,963 --> 00:25:08,798
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

479
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:10,425
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
